.TH DQL-FORMAT 1 "2026-07-05" "dql 0.1.0" "DelightQL Manual"
.SH NAME
dql-format \- format/prettify DelightQL source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dql format
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fISOURCE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Formats DelightQL source and prints the result to stdout.
.I SOURCE
is either literal source code or a path to a file containing it; if it
names a readable file the file is formatted, otherwise the argument
itself is treated as source. If
.I SOURCE
is omitted, stdin is read.
.PP
Unparseable input is refused (exit 1, "Parse error in input query").
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-color " WHEN"
Colored output:
.BR always ,
.B auto
(default: detect terminal; honors
.BR NO_COLOR ),
or
.BR never .
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-if\-not\-formatted
Print nothing; exit 1 if the input is not already formatted, 0 if it
is, 2 if the formatter cannot verify the input (see PASS-THROUGH).
For CI enforcement.
.TP
.BI \-\-highlights " FILE"
Path to a highlights.scm file.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " FILE"
Path to a theme file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success (or already formatted); 1 on parse error or, with
.BR \-\-fail\-if\-not\-formatted ,
on unformatted input; 2, with
.BR \-\-fail\-if\-not\-formatted ,
when the formatter passed the input through unverified.
.SH PASS-THROUGH
Constructs the formatter does not yet handle are passed through
byte-for-byte rather than risk corrupting code \(em but loudly: a
warning on stderr names the first unhandled construct
(\(dqformatter does not yet handle node 'pipe_operator'\(dq), and
.B \-\-fail\-if\-not\-formatted
exits 2 (\(dqcannot verify\(dq), never 0, so a CI gate can
distinguish a formatter gap from verified-formatted code.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ dql format 'a(*),b(*),a.id=b.id'
a(*), b(*), a.id = b.id
$ dql format query.dql
$ dql format --fail-if-not-formatted query.dql || echo needs formatting
.EE
.SH BUGS
Formatter coverage is incomplete: pipes
.RB ( |> ),
group-pipes
.RB ( ~> ),
and anonymous tables
.RB ( _(1,2;3,4) )
currently pass through (loudly \(em see PASS-THROUGH) instead of
being formatted. Coverage work is tracked as
bugs/cli-surface-2026-07-05/PLAN.md #3B.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dql (1),
.BR dql-query (1)
